# Website Meeting shell (org host)

Authority: `docs/platforms/website/organization-host-routing.md` §5.4–§5.5.
Linking gate / session surface: `.cursor/rules/website-meeting-live-session.mdc`.
Participant type permissions: `docs/platforms/backend/contracts/meeting-participant-domain.md` §8.

## When the shell mounts

`MeetingShell` renders header / drawer / footer / children only when `linking === "READY"`. Do not assume drawer/header run during PENDING or FAILED.

## In-shell page (`MeetingPage`)

`MeetingLayout` nests `MeetingPageProvider` under live/session providers (`useState<MeetingPage>("init")`) — same provider chain style as the other Meeting providers.

| Piece | Role |
|---|---|
| `MeetingPage` (in `useMeetingPage.tsx`) | Page id union including `"init"` |
| `MeetingDrawerPage` (local in `MeetingDrawerPanel`) | `Exclude<MeetingPage, "init">` for tile ids |
| `MeetingPageProvider` / `useMeetingPage` | Shared `page` / `setPage` for drawer + page children |
| `Meeting.tsx` | Owns the page switch — which component mounts for `page` |
| `meeting/pages/*` | In-shell page bodies (`MeetingInitPage` lobby; drawer ids → named pages, title stubs via `MeetingPageStub`) |

- One `Meeting` route only — local state, not URL segments.
- Drawer tiles call `setPage`; they do not own page rendering.
- Non-init pages may be title-only stubs (`MeetingPageStub`) until product UI ships under `meeting/pages/` — except `"attendance"`, which is shipped chair product UI.
- Do not put in-shell bodies under `ui/pages/` (route entries only). Do not invent a second route for a drawer target.

## MeetingInitPage (`"init"`)

- Shared for every `me.type`. Org logo/name + live `subject` / type / status when present.
- Attend: `can.attend` → `actions.attend` + caption `attendRequiresForRoom` under the button (no direct proxy / `batch` writes).
- Before the open window (`!attendWindow.windowOpen`): remaining-duration `attendAvailableIn` + `attendRequiresForRoom`. If the window is already open but `can.attend` is still false, show `attendRequiresForRoom` only — never a past “available in” duration. No disabled fake attend button.
- Attended: confirmation strip + first-person relative `attendedAt` + quieter `roomUnlockedHint` (`textTertiary`). Left: `leftTitle`.
- Colors only from `OrganizationColors` / `defaultOrganizationColors()`.
- Drawer `DrawerGridItem` optional accessible override prop is named `ariaLabel` (repo convention — not `a11yLabel`).

## Attendance log (`"attendance"`)

- Chairperson-only. Page owns bounce: non-chair → `setPage("init")` + render `null` (same pattern as locked `MeetingLivePage`). Data hook has no navigation side effects.
- Quorum strip only when `typeof meeting.minMembersCount === "number"` and `> 0` (hide when missing on older BLOBs — no invented default). Numerator = `CHAIRPERSON` \| `MEMBER` with bucket `present` via `countQuorumPresent`.
- Helpers + data: `hooks/useMeetingAttendance.ts` (pure bucket/sort/quorum helpers live in the same file as the hook). Filters UI: shared presentational `FilterCountChips` — page passes resolved options from the hook; no meeting translator inside the chip group. Card: `MeetingAttendanceCard.tsx` — own chrome (not `MeetingHeaderMe`).
- Page copy: single translator `meetingLayout.attendance` (incl. `title`). Do not mix `drawer` translator for the page title.
- Buckets / filter ids: `present` \| `awaiting` \| `left` (sort present → awaiting → left). Card prop: `present`.
- Absent card: `idleCardBackground` + `subtleDivider`. Present card: `presentCardBackground` + check disc (`accentActionBackground` + `accentActionText`). Type chip stays `sectionAccentBackground` (must not equal the present card fill).
- `idleCardBackground` / `presentCardBackground` live on `OrganizationColors` in `useOrganization` — do not branch `colorScheme` or reuse `sectionAccentBackground` for the present card body.
- Card rows come from the hook (`statusLabel` / `present` ready). Type label resolved inside the card from `header.type*`.
- Empty participants: `emptyParticipants` + `subtitle`. Empty filter: `emptyFilter` only (Empty default description).

## Drawer tiles (role IA)

Role from `useMeetingLiveSession().me?.type` (`CHAIRPERSON` vs other).

| Role | Tiles (order) |
|---|---|
| Chairperson | `live`, `talkQueue`, `attendance`, `agenda`, `decisionsAndVote` |
| Member / Viewer | `live`, `agenda`, `decisionsAndVote` |

- **No** `participants` tile.
- **No** `init` tile inside the role grid — `"init"` is reached via a **Home** control above the grid (`setPage("init")`, selected when `page === "init"`).
- `live` is full-row (`wide` → `gridColumn: 1 / -1`). Label copy: **Meeting room** / **غرفة الاجتماع** (`itemLive`); id stays `"live"`.
- When `!can.enterLive`, disable the `live` tile (`opc` 0.55, `aria-disabled`; `ariaLabel` / `title` = `init.attendRequiresForRoom`). Keep the visible Meeting room label. `MeetingLivePage` also bounces to `"init"` if reached while locked.
- Home control is full-row above the role grid (`itemHome` + shared `HomeMark` with white `frameClr`/`accentClr` via `actionIconOnFill`, same as drawer-menu monochrome accent override). Do not use `FiHome` or leave HomeMark orange accent on the fill well.
- Tiles call `setPage(id)` (and `onClose` on the mobile overlay); selected tile: soft `sectionAccentBackground`, partial-height start accent rail (`3px`, inset top/bottom), `textAccent` label; icon well stays `primaryActionBackground` + white `actionIconOnFill` (no selected swap, no full perimeter brand border). `aria-current="page"`.
- Tile chrome matches existing meeting drawer `DrawerGridItem` (org `OrganizationColors`, `semanticDims`).

## Header identity + request-to-speak

- Current participant cluster: `MeetingHeaderMe` (avatar + name + type chip) when `me` exists; props from session `me.name` / `me.type` / `me.avatarUrl` + org `colors`; trailing push (`pushTrailing`) so it sits before request-to-speak.
- Do **not** import `customer/IdentityAvatar` into meeting shell — compose the avatar circle with org `primaryActionBackground` and `actionIconOnFill` for the empty glyph.
- Type copy: `header.typeChairperson` / `typeMember` / `typeViewer` (`CHAIRPERSON` / `VIEWER` / else member). Visible text only — no redundant group `aria-label`.
- Name: `name.trim()` only (no invented empty-name placeholder). Cluster `maxW` uses numeric rem (`maxW={14}`), not `"14rem"`.
- Request-to-speak: show only when `me` exists and `me.type !== "CHAIRPERSON"` (MEMBER and VIEWER). Owns `ml="auto"` only when `me` is absent.
- Control is mic + visible `requestTalk` label; accessible name `requestTalkAria` (session-scoped). No switch track.
- Placeholder: disabled + `aria-disabled`; no handler.
- Chairperson manages speaking via drawer `talkQueue`, not a header control.

## Colors / Utils

- Prefer `OrganizationColors` tokens from `useOrganization` / `defaultOrganizationColors()` — including scheme pairs like `idleCardBackground` / `presentCardBackground`.
- **Create a token — do not patch.** If light/dark need different fills, or two surfaces collide visually, add a `ColorType` pair on `OrganizationColors` in `useOrganization.ts`. Forbidden: `colorScheme` / `useThemeManager` branches for meeting chrome fills; opacity hacks on the whole card; reusing `sectionAccentBackground` for a present card body when the type chip already uses it.
- Solid action wells (drawer icon squares, selected filter count on primary): glyph ink is `actionIconOnFill` (fixed `#FFFFFF`), not luminance `primaryActionText`. Accent-filled check discs use luminance `accentActionText`.
- Light-scheme `sectionBrandBackground` / `sectionAccentBackground`: `softLight` mix default **0.78** in `useOrganization` (readable chips on `pageBackground`). Do not wash toward 0.92; do not hardcode chip fills in page code. Present attendance card fill uses `presentCardBackground` (`softLight` **0.62** / `softDark` **0.18**).
- `As={"button"}`: `baseCssStyle` = `...ElementStyles.buttonReset` only when every state sets `bg` (incl. `"@transparent"`). Use `background: "transparent"` in `baseCssStyle` **only** with `bg={selected ? fill : undefined}`. `fontVariantNumeric` / overflow scroll live in `cssStyle`.
- Menu glyph may keep `semanticColor.iconPrimary` on `DrawerMenuIcon` (shared with customer shell mark).
- Meeting Home `HomeMark`: pass `frameClr` + `accentClr` = `actionIconOnFill` so the orange floor rail does not appear on the primary fill well.
